00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:06.000
<b>Report</b>

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:06.000
<b>Oobayashi Yukiko</b>

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:09.000
Currently, the shutters are closed,
and we cannot go inside to inquire—

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:15.210
The self-diagnosis program reports issues 
across 1345 areas. 7% of the mainframe is bent,

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:18.010
12 of the motors burnt out, 
8 of them with abnormal readings.

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:22.510
Gotta replace the hatch and the right arm, 
and the battery's fried, too.

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:26.270
It stood its ground pretty well, 
despite the beating that it took.

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:27.520
He put up a good fight.

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:29.310
Now the problem's this.

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:35.030
We gotta set up <i>three</i> industrial robots 
by this weekend? Talk about impossible. 

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:37.820
We'll be tied to this for ten days without Gramps.

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:40.820
I guess Jet Jaguar will have to wait.

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:42.320
Forget about those scraps.

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:44.740
He said to get a move on 
and be ready for the next fight.

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:46.410
Satomi.

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:48.910
How's Gramps doing?

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:51.750
Fit as a fiddle. He'll be discharged next week.

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:55.250
He'll probably get kicked out of the hospital
with all that ruckus he's making.

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:57.170
But never mind that,
 he told me you guys need to see this.

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:58.800
The hell's that?

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:01.550
The flying one appears to be that pterodactyl.

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:03.260
"Those bastards'll be back!"

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:06.310
"There are more of 'em drawn here, 
so its friends will come!"

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:08.140
"Next time, it'll be a whole bastard flock of 'em!"

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:11.060
"Ya gotta get Jet Jaguar running by then!"

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:13.650
That pterodactyl... are they similar?

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:16.730
This is the same painting that was on display in 
front of the station during the festival.

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:18.190
"Illustration of Koshira?"

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:20.360
Apparently, it's "Godzilla."

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:23.410
It's a local legend that's withstood the test of time.

