00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:35.630
Chinzei

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:35.630
Ouetsu

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:37.670
What do you think? Nonsense or what?

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:40.880
I mean, Gramps' hunches are rarely off.

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:45.300
Even if he told us to fix up Jet Jaguar, 
the parts we'll need won't arrive until next week.

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:49.480
Assuming we fix him, what hope 
does he have against a swarm of them?

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:51.640
We're not completely in the dark should that happen.

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:58.030
Is that its screech?

00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:00.190
Jet Jaguar recorded it.

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:01.400
As for this...

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:07.740
That's the radio waves it's emitting?

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:10.750
The very same ones we picked 
up at the haunted house.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:12.960
It emits radio waves along with its screeches.

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:16.750
Furthermore, the neon billboard it 
crashed into emitted a high frequency.

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:19.420
You're saying its radio waves 
are what drew in the monster?

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:22.220
Assuming it's a creature that 
communicates through radio waves...

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:26.010
We have a lead—we might be able 
to produce a signal to lure them in.

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:27.430
Makes sense.

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:30.850
But what do we do once we lure them in?

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:35.060
Who knows. How about we shepherd 
them into the sea like the Pied Piper?

