The ex-ex director showed it to me, and it seems to be a story passed down from director to director.

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:48.990
It isn't a duty that's passed between 
directors or anything of the sort.

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:52.790
You hear stories like this all the time, don't you?

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:54.420
Urban myths, and such.

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:58.340
Myths like the mummies of kappas 
that were sealed away in temples.

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:00.050
It got deserted?

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:02.510
I'd hardly consider <i>that</i> to be something we should ignore.

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:06.430
Satou—our job is to observe radio waves.

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:08.350
Dinosaur bones are beyond our area of expertise.

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:13.100
Besides, we don't want a big fuss 
over what's buried down there.

