00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:13.510
The radio wave kaiju Rodan?

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:24.140
A response to a paper? Whose?

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:28.400
A "Professor Li" has sent an email 
regarding your paper that I published!

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:31.020
<i>My </i>paper? Really?

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:33.440
Why are you refrigerating an empty bottle?

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:38.070
Please search: ingredients for mentsuyu.
It's soy sauce, sugar, and...?

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:39.490
Mirin and dashi.

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:40.740
Dashi, was it...

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:42.160
How do I make katsuobushi?

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:44.660
The process takes a year at the very least.

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:46.160
Can I use ketchup instead?

00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:50.590
Tomato's umami flavor comes from glutamate,
while katsuobushi's comes from inosic acid.

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:54.420
What if we try distillation? Or chromatography?

00:17:55.670 --> 00:17:57.380
Oh, shoot!

00:17:57.380 --> 00:17:59.090
Hot, hot, hot!

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:00.760
You boiled it for 60 seconds too long.

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:03.560
You're 60 seconds too late in informing me!

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:07.350
Hey, where were we at again?

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:11.520
There was a response to your paper 
that I uploaded to the preprint server.

00:18:11.940 --> 00:18:13.690
Paper? <i>Mine?</i>

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:15.320
Behold!

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:18.110
"Introduction to Biologia Phantastica."

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:21.330
Mei Kamino. Co-written by Pelops II.

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:22.830
You made this on your own!?

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:25.450
I included my name as co-author, too!

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:27.830
This is what you call co-research, indeed.

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:33.500
"A discussion on fantastical creatures that go against the 
flow of time and the law of physics concerned, as well as..."

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:37.170
It reads more like a compilation 
of science essays than a paper...

00:18:37.170 --> 00:18:38.180
What even is this?

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:39.890
This is your notes compiled.

00:18:39.890 --> 00:18:42.220
I published it after a good polish!

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:46.980
I mean, it's super polished and all, but...

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:48.100
How do I put it...

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:55.440
Since publishing, there have been 32 comments on the title, 
5 downloads, and 1 email response within 20 hours!

00:18:48.110 --> 00:19:04.120
----------------------

00:18:48.110 --> 00:19:04.120
Comments

00:18:48.110 --> 00:19:04.120
----------------------

00:18:48.110 --> 00:19:04.120
Downloads

00:18:48.110 --> 00:19:04.120
----------------------

00:18:48.110 --> 00:19:04.120
Email Response

00:18:55.440 --> 00:18:56.400
An email response?

00:18:56.400 --> 00:19:00.700
Someone called Professor Li 
emailed you regarding your paper.

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:03.120
She would like to meet with 
you in Tokyo and discuss further.

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:04.120
Who does?

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:08.750
Professor Li! The one who sent you an email 
and wants to meet up with you.

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:10.620
Microfiches.

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:13.040
They supposedly last for 100 years,

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:15.500
and these may just be about that old.

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:20.130
Old Tsuguno District Management Organization?

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:21.590
"Ashihara..." 

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:23.140
The name rings a bell.

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:26.970
It's Ashihara Michiyuki. The founder of this facility.

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:29.180
Oh, really? Aren't you well informed.

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:35.110
An alarm?

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:39.490
It's a fairly old relic, 
and we can't tell exactly what it's for.

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:45.620
But it was connected to a machine underground 
where there's a giant dinosaur skeleton.

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:48.500
A dinosaur? What kind of fairy tale is that?

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:50.660
Listen, it's a long story.

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:52.080
Satou...

00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:53.080
Yeah?

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:55.340
Can you summarize that in a report?

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:02.970
A dinosaur skeleton underground?

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:04.930
I hope he doesn't have a screw loose.

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:10.520
Professor Li.

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:13.100
She specializes in computational chemistry.

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:17.230
Computational chemistry—a branch of chemistry 
that uses simulations to discover new molecules.

00:20:17.230 --> 00:20:19.570
Is that not related to your research?

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:23.240
The professor's molecular simulations only
utilize existing principles of reality.

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:28.790
Ultralight, ultratough, 
ultraductile, ultraflexible, ultraconductive...

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:31.370
Seems she's searching for 
molecules with a variety of properties.

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:33.750
It doesn't seem like she succeeded 
in synthesizing any of them, though.

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:35.040
SHIVA?

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:39.760
The professor is currently 
collaborating with SHIVA Consortium.

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:46.720
How's that?

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:51.390
Gyro Canopy Tandem 2, 
installed with the Special Anti-Rodan Antenna

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:53.640
In short, Gyro Z!

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:56.440
Exactly how is it shortened to have that name?

00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:58.400
Gramps!

00:20:58.900 --> 00:20:59.940
Yo!

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:02.400
Y'all seem ready and rarin' to go.

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:04.400
You're not an accident waiting to happen?

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:08.160
You fool! This is no time for me to stay bedridden.

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:14.710
We were catching endless shoals of deep-sea fish yesterday.

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:17.170
And yet, there hasn't been a single bite today.

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:19.750
Rather than chasing after fish that have gone home...

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:22.170
...we should be back on land selling Rodan manju.

00:21:22.710 --> 00:21:23.510
Did you see that!?

00:21:23.510 --> 00:21:25.430
Th... That's—

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:39.650
It's...

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:40.900
Rodan?

00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:43.690
Th-This is trouble.

00:22:06.470 --> 00:22:12.220
<b>I woke up to your voice that painted my vision with color</b>

00:22:12.220 --> 00:22:18.100
<b>And it was the same shade of curiosity I find in my familiar daily life</b>

00:22:18.100 --> 00:22:23.480
<b>If this feeling can grow naturally on its own</b>

00:22:23.480 --> 00:22:29.360
<b>Will it fall off one day like an unripe fruit, I wonder? </b>

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:33.990
<b>I don't know anything</b>

00:22:33.990 --> 00:22:38.370
<b>Not even anything about you</b>

00:22:41.250 --> 00:22:46.880
<b>Let me keep on dreaming for now</b>

00:22:46.880 --> 00:22:51.260
<b>If this moment is all I have now</b>

00:22:51.720 --> 00:22:55.720
<b>I can still feel the warmth in my palm</b>

00:22:57.560 --> 00:23:02.980
<b>My thrumming feelings open and burst out</b>

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:06.990
<b>I want to keep learning more, like I am now</b>

00:23:08.740 --> 00:23:13.530
<b>This pulsating rhythm I feel just won't stop</b>

00:23:13.530 --> 00:23:14.490
<b>It won't stop</b>
